IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Part V: reg 92, Direct Deposit of Benefits.
-- Piece er5, LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Every `src:N` is a line of SOR-96-332.txt. The text is an unofficial rendering;
-- nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld): reg 92(2) is the claimant's claim to have benefits deposited directly (the Commission bears the duty), qualified by the Commission's
-- power, in (7), to refuse access (the claimant is liable to it); reg 92(3) and (5) put duties on the claimant; reg 92(4) is a rule of evidence in the claimant's
-- favour; reg 92(8) is the Commission's power to redirect a deposit (the claimant is liable to it unless they advise otherwise).
-- Section 38 of the Act is piece ei2's and section 135 is piece ei4's; neither is encoded here.
-- The Direct Deposit Regulations (reg 92(1)) are not among the inputs: what their sections 2 and 4 to 8 say is not encoded, and reg 92(1) is carried as the list of
-- section numbers it names.

§ `Regulations Part V - Direct Deposit of Benefits`

§§ `Reg 92(1) - the Direct Deposit Regulations`

-- For the purposes of this section, sections 2 and 4 to 8 of the Direct Deposit Regulations apply. Their text is not among the inputs, so only the section numbers are carried.
-- src:1698 | 92 (1) For the purposes of this section, sections 2 and 4 to 8 of the Direct Deposit Regulations apply.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 92(1) (src:1698)
`reg 92(1) the sections of the Direct Deposit Regulations that apply for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    LIST 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8

§§ `Reg 92(2) - benefits deposited directly`

-- Subject to subsection (7), a claimant shall have their benefits deposited directly to their bank account if the claimant has provided the Commission with the number of an active account
-- registered in the claimant's name in a financial institution in Canada. Subsection (7) is the right to refuse a person access to the electronic systems used for direct deposit.
-- src:1699 | (2) Subject to subsection (7), a claimant shall have their benefits deposited directly to their bank account if the claimant has provided the Commission with the number of an active account registered in the claimant's name in a financial institution in Canada.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 92(2) (src:1699)
GIVEN `the claimant has provided the Commission with the number of an account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the account is active` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the account is registered in the claimant's name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the account is in a financial institution in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has been refused access to the electronic systems used for the direct deposit of benefits under subsection 92(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(2) the claimant's benefits are to be deposited directly to their bank account` IF
        `the claimant has provided the Commission with the number of an account`
    AND `the account is active`
    AND `the account is registered in the claimant's name`
    AND `the account is in a financial institution in Canada`
    AND (NOT `the claimant has been refused access to the electronic systems used for the direct deposit of benefits under subsection 92(7)`)

§§ `Reg 92(3) - responsibility for the data`

-- A claimant is responsible for the accuracy of the data supplied by the claimant in order to register for the direct deposit of benefits.
-- src:1700 | (3) A claimant is responsible for the accuracy of the data supplied by the claimant in order to register for the direct deposit of benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 92(3) (src:1700)
GIVEN `the data is supplied by the claimant in order to register for the direct deposit of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(3) the claimant is responsible for the accuracy of the data` IF
    `the data is supplied by the claimant in order to register for the direct deposit of benefits`

§§ `Reg 92(4) - evidence of the transfer and the payment`

-- In the absence of any evidence to the contrary, the two documents together constitute evidence of the transfer of funds to a claimant's account and the payment of benefits to the claimant:
-- (a) a document certified by a person acting for the Commission to be an extract from the record authorizing a direct deposit transaction in respect of the claimant to be directed to the financial institution where the claimant's account is located; and
-- (b) a certified extract of the records of that financial institution indicating the crediting of the amount of the deposit to the account of the claimant.
-- The text says what the two documents are worth when there is no evidence to the contrary. It does not say that nothing else is evidence, nor what they are worth against contrary evidence,
-- so those cases return NOTHING (not covered).
-- src:1701 | (4) In the absence of any evidence to the contrary, the following documents together constitute evidence of the transfer of funds to a claimant's account and the payment of benefits to the claimant:
-- src:1702 | (a) a document certified by a person acting for the Commission to be an extract from the record authorizing a direct deposit transaction, in respect of the claimant, to be directed to the financial institution where the account of the claimant is located; and
-- src:1703 | (b) a certified extract of the records of that financial institution indicating the crediting of the amount of the deposit to the account of the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 92(4) (src:1701-1703)
GIVEN `there is no evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a document certified by a person acting for the Commission to be an extract from the record authorizing a direct deposit transaction in respect of the claimant to be directed to the financial institution where the claimant's account is located` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a certified extract of the records of that financial institution indicating the crediting of the amount of the deposit to the account of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(4) the documents together constitute evidence of the transfer of funds and the payment of benefits` IS
    IF     `there is no evidence to the contrary`
       AND `there is a document certified by a person acting for the Commission to be an extract from the record authorizing a direct deposit transaction in respect of the claimant to be directed to the financial institution where the claimant's account is located`
       AND `there is a certified extract of the records of that financial institution indicating the crediting of the amount of the deposit to the account of the claimant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Reg 92(5) - ending the direct deposit`

-- In order to terminate the direct deposit of benefits, the claimant shall notify the Commission: the deposit ends only when the claimant has notified it.
-- src:1704 | (5) In order to terminate the direct deposit of benefits, the claimant shall notify the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 92(5) (src:1704)
GIVEN `the claimant wishes to terminate the direct deposit of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(5) the claimant must notify the Commission` IF
    `the claimant wishes to terminate the direct deposit of benefits`

-- src:1704 | (5) In order to terminate the direct deposit of benefits, the claimant shall notify the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 92(5) (src:1704)
GIVEN `the claimant wishes to terminate the direct deposit of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has notified the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(5) the direct deposit of benefits is terminated` IF
        `the claimant wishes to terminate the direct deposit of benefits`
    AND `the claimant has notified the Commission`

§§ `Reg 92(6) and (7) - sections 38 and 135 of the Act and the electronic systems`

-- For greater certainty, sections 38 and 135 of the Act apply to declarations made in the context of the payment of benefits under this section.
-- src:1705 | (6) For greater certainty, sections 38 and 135 of the Act apply to declarations made in the context of the payment of benefits under this section.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 92(6) (src:1705)
GIVEN `the declaration is made in the context of the payment of benefits under regulation 92` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(6) sections 38 and 135 of the Act apply to the declaration` IF
    `the declaration is made in the context of the payment of benefits under regulation 92`

-- The acts and omissions in ss 38(1) and 135(1) of the Act are deemed to include those of a person who knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used
-- for the direct deposit of benefits; the penalty in s 38(2) and the punishment in s 135(3) are deemed to include the right to refuse access to those systems to such a person.
-- src:1706 | (7) The acts and omissions specified in subsections 38(1) and 135(1) of the Act are deemed to include the acts or omissions of a person who knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used for the direct deposit of benefits, and the penalty provided for by subsection 38(2) of the Act and the punishment provided for by subsection 135(3) of the Act are deemed to include the right to refuse access to those electronic systems to such a person.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 92(7) (src:1706)
GIVEN `the person knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used for the direct deposit of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(7) the act is deemed to be an act or omission specified in subsections 38(1) and 135(1) of the Act` IF
    `the person knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used for the direct deposit of benefits`

-- src:1706 | (7) The acts and omissions specified in subsections 38(1) and 135(1) of the Act are deemed to include the acts or omissions of a person who knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used for the direct deposit of benefits, and the penalty provided for by subsection 38(2) of the Act and the punishment provided for by subsection 135(3) of the Act are deemed to include the right to refuse access to those electronic systems to such a person.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 92(7) (src:1706)
GIVEN `the person knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used for the direct deposit of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(7) the penalty and the punishment include the right to refuse the person access to the electronic systems used for direct deposit` IF
    `the person knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used for the direct deposit of benefits`

§§ `Reg 92(8) - redirecting the deposit`

-- Unless otherwise advised by the claimant, the Commission may redirect the deposit of benefits from an active account at a financial institution, the number of which was provided to the Commission
-- by the claimant, to another financial institution, branch or active account number when the financial institution notifies the Commission of a change of the financial institution, branch or account number.
-- src:1707 | (8) Unless otherwise advised by the claimant, the Commission may redirect the deposit of benefits from an active account at a financial institution the number of which was provided to the Commission by the claimant to another financial institution, branch or active account number when the financial institution notifies the Commission of a change of the financial institution, branch or account number.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 92(8) (src:1707)
GIVEN `the claimant has otherwise advised the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deposit is made to an active account at a financial institution, the number of which the claimant provided to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial institution has notified the Commission of a change of the financial institution, branch or account number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(8) the Commission may redirect the deposit of benefits` IF
        (NOT `the claimant has otherwise advised the Commission`)
    AND `the deposit is made to an active account at a financial institution, the number of which the claimant provided to the Commission`
    AND `the financial institution has notified the Commission of a change of the financial institution, branch or account number`
